    "Reduce forecast peak values after sharp upward spikes (e.g., >75% above recent mean) to prevent overshoot.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias correction: if forecast deviates >±10% from 30-day moving average, adjust toward historical mean.",
    "For 30-day horizon, penalize overconfidence in early periods (e.g., first 5 days) if sentiment is low — reduce initial forecast slope.",
    "If sentiment is positive (≥0.33) and forecast is consistently below true outcome, increase forecast by 2–5% to capture sentiment-driven momentum."
